        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Coastal feedstocks and inland connections",
        "content": "Different locations reveal different industrial relationships. Arya Sasol’s technical catalogue places its ethylene and polyethylene operations at Assaluyeh in Bushehr Province, on the Persian Gulf. The catalogue describes an integrated sequence in which an ethane cracker supplies ethylene to downstream polyethylene units. This is evidence of a documented plant configuration, not confirmation of present operating rates. [s4]\n\nIsfahan offers another model. Encyclopaedia Iranica records that its refinery-linked petrochemical plant began operation in 1992 and produced aromatic chemicals for several downstream uses. Read together, these examples show why an account of Iran’s chemical geography must include both gas-related coastal complexes and inland refinery connections. The historical Isfahan description should not be mistaken for a current production inventory. [s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s4"]
      },
      {
        "id": "performance",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Measuring performance carefully",
        "content": "Feedstock availability connects chemical production to the wider energy system. The U.S. Energy Information Administration’s 2024 assessment describes competition among industrial, electricity, residential, and commercial gas users, together with inadequate storage for seasonal demand. Large reserves therefore do not automatically imply uninterrupted industrial supply. [s3]\n\nS&P Global reported in 2025 that feedstock shortages were leaving petrochemical capacity unused, citing the deputy oil minister responsible for petrochemical affairs. This supports distinguishing installed capacity from actual production. Its account of investment requirements and projects also concerns financing needs and planned development, not independently verified completion. [s5]\n\nFor readers exploring the sector, the useful questions are concrete: what material is being produced, what production stage does it represent, which customers use it, and does a reported figure describe capacity, output, or sales? Those distinctions provide a firmer basis for comparison than an undifferentiated national tonnage total. [s1][s4][s5]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s3", "s4", "s5"]
      }
    ],
